LLM Response:
-----------------------------------------------------------
Text:
The Contact Protection Boxes CD-P11 and CD-P12 are designed to protect relay contacts from surges that occur with AC inductive loads (omron-c-family-relays-datasheet.pdf, page 10). For DC loads, a diode is generally more effective (omron-c-family-relays-datasheet.pdf, page 10).

**Key Specifications:**
*   **Applicable Voltage:** 100 to 120 VAC or 200 to 240 VAC (omron-c-family-relays-datasheet.pdf, page 10).
*   **Applicable Contact Current:** 0.1 to 1 A (omron-c-family-relays-datasheet.pdf, page 10).
*   **Ambient Operating Temperature:** -25°C to 60°C (omron-c-family-relays-datasheet.pdf, page 10).
*   **Leakage Current:** There is a leakage current of approximately 1 mA at 100 VAC and 2 mA at 200 VAC. If the load current is smaller than this leakage current, the relay may not turn off (omron-c-family-relays-datasheet.pdf, page 10).

These models are approved by UL, CSA, and TÜV (EN 60947-5-1) standards (omron-c-family-relays-datasheet.pdf, page 10).
